From e9acd823db72901091530df2caf6b65378ad782e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahriar Iravanian <siravan@svtsim.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:59:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] rusticol: pacman feature, arena capture and external
 runner

New cargo feature `pacman` (implies `tile-override`, adds libloading):
- PACMAN_SAVE_ARENA=DIR captures compiled-direct arenas, schedules and kernels
  for replay by symjit-utils' `pacman` tool;
- PACMAN_RUNNER=DIR loads runner libraries built by `pacman runner [--cuda]`
  (C ABI) and runs the compiled schedule through them, e.g. on a CUDA GPU;
  every engine then uses the RUSTICOL_TILE_POINTS tile.
Without the feature, or without the variables, nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
